%N A402782 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} exp(-k) * sigma(k)/k, where sigma(k) = A000203(k) is the sum of divisors of k.
%H A402782 Maxie Dion Schmidt, <a href="https://doi.org/10.61091/ojac21-01">A catalog of interesting and useful Lambert series identities</a>, Online Journal of Analytic Combinatorics, Issue 21 (2026), Paper #1, pp. 1-22, p. 10, eq. (4c); <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.02976">arXiv preprint</a>, arXiv:2004.02976 [math.NT], 2020-2026, p. 9, eq. (2.1c).
%H A402782 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/LambertSeries.html">Lambert Series</a>, eq. (17).
%F A402782 Equals Sum_{k>=1} (A017665(k)/A017666(k))/exp(k).
%F A402782 Equals -log(A292902).
%F A402782 Equals -Sum_{k>=1} log(1 - exp(-k)).
%F A402782 Equals Sum_{k>=1} 1/(k * (exp(k)-1)).
%F A402782 Equals Integral_{x>=1} floor(x)/(exp(x)-1) dx.
%F A402782 Equals zeta(2) - log(2*Pi)/2 - 1/24 - Sum_{k>=1} log(1 - exp(-4*Pi^2*k)) (the absolute value of the sum is less than 10^(-17)).
%e A402782 0.684328866976887035182584598759782095894025446164807...
%t A402782 RealDigits[Log[QPochhammer[E^(-1)]], 10, 105][[1]]
%o A402782 (PARI) suminf(k = 1, -log(1 - exp(-k)))
%Y A402782 Cf. A000203, A013661, A017665, A017666, A061444, A292902.
%Y A402782 Sum_{k>=1} sigma(k)/f(k): A066766 (2^k), A084254 (k*exp(2*Pi*k)), A183699 (k^3), A183700 (k^4), A227988 (k!), A255695 (k*exp(Pi*k)), A255697 (k*exp(4*Pi*k)), A335764 (k*2^k), A367325 (2^k-1), A397451 (k^4/log(k)), A398700 (k^2*(k+1)), this constant (k*e^k).
